Here is a complete, secure `login.php` script.

It uses **Prepared Statements** (prevents SQL Injection), **`password_verify()`** (handles secure password hashing like bcrypt/argon2), **Session Regeneration** (prevents Session Fixation), and **`httpOnly`/`Secure` cookie flags** (mitigates XSS).

### `login.php`

```php
<?php
// 1. Configuration & Setup
require_once 'config.php'; // See below for what this should contain

// 2. Only process POST requests
if ($_SERVER['REQUEST_METHOD'] !== 'POST') {
    header('Location: login.php');
    exit;
}

// 3. Collect & Sanitize Input
$username = trim($_POST['username'] ?? '');
$password = $_POST['password'] ?? ''; // Do NOT trim passwords (spaces can be valid)

$errors = [];

if (empty($username)) {
    $errors[] = 'Username is required.';
}
if (empty($password)) {
    $errors[] = 'Password is required.';
}

// 4. Database Lookup & Verification
if (empty($errors)) {
    try {
        // SQL: Select specific columns (avoid SELECT *)
        $sql = "SELECT id, username, password_hash FROM users WHERE username = :username LIMIT 1";
        $stmt = $pdo->prepare($sql);
        $stmt->execute([':username' => $username]);
        $user = $stmt->fetch(PDO::FETCH_ASSOC);

        // Verify user exists AND password matches
        // password_verify handles the hash comparison securely (timing safe)
        if ($user && password_verify($password, $user['password_hash'])) {

            // 5. SUCCESS: Secure Session Handling

            // Regenerate ID to prevent Session Fixation attacks
            session_regenerate_id(true);

            // Store minimal necessary data in session
            $_SESSION['user_id']    = (int)$user['id'];
            $_SESSION['username']   = $user['username'];
            $_SESSION['logged_in']  = true;
            $_SESSION['last_activity'] = time(); // Optional: for idle timeout logic

            // 6. Redirect to Dashboard
            header('Location: dashboard.php');
            exit;

        } else {
            // Generic error message (Don't reveal if user exists or not)
            $errors[] = 'Invalid username or password.';
        }

    } catch (PDOException $e) {
        // Log the actual error server-side, show generic message to user
        error_log("Login DB Error: " . $e->getMessage());
        $errors[] = 'A system error occurred. Please try again later.';
    }
}

// 7. FAILURE: Redirect back to login with errors
// We store errors in session to survive the redirect (PRG Pattern)
$_SESSION['login_errors'] = $errors;
// Preserve username input so user doesn't have to retype it (optional)
$_SESSION['old_username'] = $username; 

header('Location: login.php');
exit;
```

